# Yarr Plex / Tautulli

## Gate

Use when the user asks about Plex libraries/sessions or Tautulli
activity/history/stats via yarr MCP. Skip *arr library adds and qBit
queue work. Always load `yarr-safety` for writes/deletes.

Never invent Plex rating keys, library section ids, or Tautulli user ids.
Resolve from MCP reads or user paste.

## Prefer MCP

When a yarr MCP is ready (`user-mcp_yarr`):

### `plex`

Actions: `service_status`, `api_get`, `api_post`, `api_put`, `api_delete`,
`help`, `codemode`, `op`, `snippet_list`, `snippet_save`, `snippet_run`,
`snippet_delete`.

### `tautulli`

Same shared actions, plus stats helpers:

| Action | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `stats_activity` | Current activity / sessions |
| `stats_history` | Watch history |
| `stats_users` | User stats |
| `stats_libraries` | Library stats |
| `stats_refresh_libraries` | Refresh library cache — mutate gate |
| `stats_refresh_users` | Refresh user cache — mutate gate |
| `stats_delete_image_cache` | Destructive cache clear — explicit verb |

Useful params when the schema exposes them: `user`, `page`, `page_size`,
`period`, `start`, `length`, `timezone`.

## Read defaults

1. `service_status` on `plex` / `tautulli` before deep API calls.
2. Prefer Tautulli `stats_*` read actions for "who's watching" /
   history over raw Plex API dumps.
3. Prefer `api_get` with a resolved path over guessing Plex XML endpoints.
4. Summarize sessions (user, title, player) — do not paste tokens or full
   device identifiers when a short summary answers the ask.

## Mutates

Require an explicit verb this turn (`yarr-safety`) for:

- Plex `api_post` / `api_put` / `api_delete` (library edits, item delete)
- Tautulli `stats_refresh_*` and `stats_delete_image_cache`
- Mutating `op` / `snippet_run` / `snippet_delete` / `snippet_save`

Prefer read/search. Refuse bulk library wipes without a named target.

## Report shape

- Tool (`plex` / `tautulli`) + action
- Session/library/user summary (ids only when needed)
- Explicit note when mutate refused

## Out of scope

- *arr grab/search (see `yarr-arr`)
- Seerr approvals (see `yarr-seerr`)
- qBit torrent ops (see `yarr-qbit`)

